  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1255 AM CDT Sat Oct 10 2026\n\nThe track of Isaias remains well east of our region, and the main \neffect of this track for our area is good chances of showers and \nsome thunderstorms, and an increase in winds this afternoon and \nevening. The model blend produces 40-90% chances today into \ntonight across all but our far western counties in southeast \nMissouri, and has backed off a little more on our potential wind\ngusts this afternoon and evening to 25 to around 30 mph. \nRainfall totals range from around a quarter inch or less across \nmost of southern Illinois and extreme south Missouri, to a half \ninch or less in southwest Indiana, to around an inch in west \nKentucky and extreme southeast Illinois. Precipitation will \ngradually end from west to east late this evening through Sunday\nmorning, with mostly sunny to sunny skies across our entire \nregion by Sunday afternoon.\n\nThe return of sunshine Sunday will also bring the return of well \nabove normal temperatures, especially across the western two-thirds \nof the PAH forecast area. Winds will shift back to the south \nlate Sunday into Sunday night, and high temperatures Monday and \nTuesday will reach near record to record readings the upper 80s \nto around 90 degrees.\n\nModels show an unsettled pattern setting up for mid to late week, \nwith a frontal boundary sinking south into our region Tuesday night \ninto Wednesday, lingering in the vicinity, followed by a late week \ncold front. Timing and location are still in question, but this will \nbring an end to the record heat and give our area on and off \nchances of showers and some thunderstorms late Tuesday night \nthrough Thursday night, potentially lingering into Friday. \nChances are overall in the 20-50% range through this period, but\nas timing gets a little more defined, we could see some periods\nwith better chances. As mentioned, this pattern will bring \ntemperatures down, but readings will still be well above normal \nwith highs in the upper 70s to middle 80s Tuesday through \nThursday, with lows in the 60s. Normal highs by that time are \nthe lower to middle 70s and lows are the middle to upper 40s. If\nthe late week cold front timing pans out, more seasonable \nconditions will arrive Friday.",
